@startuml cls-attendance
title Class Diagram — Attendance

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class ClassSession <<external — scheduling>> {
}
class AcademicActor <<external — academic>> {
}
class School <<external — academic>> {
}
class Cohort <<external — academic>> {
}
class AppUser <<external — identity>> {
}

enum AttendanceStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Present
  Absent
  Late
  Justified
}

enum CaptureMethod <<enumeration>> {
  FACIAL
  MANUAL
  IOT
  IMPORT
}

enum ReviewStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Pending
  Approved
  Rejected
}

class AttendanceRecord {
  +attendanceRecordId: Long
  +classSessionId: Long
  +academicActorId: Long
  +attendanceStatus: AttendanceStatus
  +capturedAt: DateTime
  +captureMethod: CaptureMethod
  +matchScore: Decimal
  +record()
}

class JustificationType {
  +justificationTypeId: Int
  +schoolId: Int
  +name: String
  +description: String
  +requiresAttachment: Boolean
  +status: Boolean
}

class Justification {
  +justificationId: Long
  +attendanceRecordId: Long
  +justificationTypeId: Int
  +reason: String
  +submittedAt: DateTime
  +reviewedBy: UUID
  +reviewedAt: DateTime
  +reviewStatus: ReviewStatus
  +resolutionNotes: String
  +submit()
  +review(decision)
}

class SupportingDocument {
  +supportingDocumentId: Long
  +justificationId: Long
  +fileName: String
  +storageUri: String
  +mimeType: String
  +sizeBytes: Long
  +upload()
}

class AttendanceReport <<derived projection, no FKs>> {
  +reportId: UUID
  +schoolId: Int
  +cohortId: Long
  +generatedBy: UUID
  +reportType: String
  +filters: JSON
  +result: JSON
  +generatedAt: DateTime
}

AttendanceRecord "1" -- "0..1" Justification : justification.attendance_record_id FK\nUNIQUE one-to-one
JustificationType "1" -- "0..*" Justification : justification.justification_type_id FK
Justification "1" -- "0..*" SupportingDocument : supporting_document.justification_id FK
AttendanceRecord --> AttendanceStatus
AttendanceRecord --> CaptureMethod
Justification --> ReviewStatus

AttendanceRecord ..> ClassSession : class_session_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
AttendanceRecord ..> AcademicActor : academic_actor_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
Justification ..> AppUser : reviewed_by\n(cross-context, no FK)
AttendanceReport ..> School : school_id\n(no FK, derived projection)
AttendanceReport ..> Cohort : cohort_id\n(no FK, derived projection)
AttendanceReport ..> AppUser : generated_by\n(no FK, derived projection)

note right of AttendanceRecord
  RN-22: one record per academic_actor per
  class_session (uq_attendance_session_actor),
  the only real guard -- RecordAttendanceUseCaseImpl
  only depends on AttendanceRecordRepository, so
  RN-23 (the session must be Open) is NOT checked
  server-side (corrected 2026-10-12 against FULL/):
  a record can be written against a Closed or
  Cancelled class_session with no error. Absent
  records leave capturedAt NULL. Only
  captureMethod=MANUAL is wired for the alternative
  path (RN-26) — FACIAL capture is designed but no
  client calls the write yet, see SEQ-01.
end note

note left of JustificationType
  school_id NULL = global type.
  uq_justification_type_school_name plus a
  partial unique on name WHERE school_id IS NULL.
end note

note right of Justification
  RN-32: exactly one justification per
  attendance_record (1:1, UNIQUE). Review is a
  one-shot transition: Pending -> Approved or
  Rejected only, a resolved justification cannot
  be reviewed again (corrected 2026-10-12 against
  FULL/). RN-33 IS enforced: approving a type
  that requires an attachment 400s unless a
  SupportingDocument row exists -- it only checks
  the row exists, not that its file was really
  uploaded (see the SupportingDocument note).
  RN-36 (intended): approval should cascade
  attendance_status to Justified
  -- it does not (see ST-02 / SEQ-03). See
  act-justification-process.mmd for the full
  intended-vs-real process.
end note

note bottom of SupportingDocument
  Both Web and Mobile call this endpoint with
  real metadata right after a justification is
  created, but storageUri is fabricated
  client-side -- no multipart upload, no MinIO
  or S3 SDK call exists anywhere, ADR-009 was
  never implemented. The row is real, the file
  it names was never transmitted. See SEQ-03.
end note

note as N1
  All classes also carry the standard audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted
  here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and
  06-data/domains/05-attendance.md for the
  column-level ER view. Biometric entities
  (FacialEmbedding, FingerprintEmbedding,
  BiometricUpdateCase) live in
  cls-biometric.puml — ms-attendance never calls
  ms-biometric directly, see SEQ-01.
end note

@enduml
